module

public import Theory.Mathieu.M24.LocalGeometry.EvenCatalogue.Coverage.Operations

/-!
# Finite witnesses for normal elementary catalogue coverage

The generator in `source/generate.py` finds short products of conjugates to
exclude 880 entries, and to recover the normal closure generators of each of
the remaining 143 nonidentity entries. Joining any two catalogue entries
either stays inside the larger row, gives a higher row, or produces an element
whose square is nonidentity. The separate checking modules prove every identity
used; these data carry no trusted group-theoretic assertions.

Source context: Aschbacher–Smith, condition E, printed pp.3–4; GLS3 Table 5.3e.
-/

@[expose] public section
namespace Sporadic.Mathieu.M24LocalGeometry.EvenCatalogue.Coverage
open SylowNormalizer OrderEnumeration
set_option maxRecDepth 100000

